ng too faithful (which draws murders) or too suspicious (which draws banishments). The 60% traitor win rate combined with these survival patterns indicates that social manipulation and relationship-building trump pure deductive reasoning in this simulation, creating a game where the best liars and social networkers consistently outperform the most logical players."
